# Line endings are part of a contract here, not a preference.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES, measured 2026-08-19 on run 32288856529: `unit
# (windows-latest)` failed 8 tests across gen_client_golden_test.dart and
# doc_fixture_client_golden_test.dart, every one of them
#
#     Expected: '// GENERATED CODE - DO NOT MODIFY BY HAND\n'
#       Actual: '// GENERATED CODE - DO NOT MODIFY BY HAND\r\n'
#
# The goldens ARE the committed files (apps/playground/lib/gen/**), compared
# byte for byte against what the generator would emit. The generator writes
# LF on every platform; Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so the
# checkout handed the test CRLF. Nothing was wrong with either side -- they
# were reading different bytes than were committed.
#
# Fixed here rather than by normalising inside the tests, because the tests are
# not the only reader. `zonai gen client --check` compares the same way
# (client_generator.dart, `check`), so the same skew is a real defect for a
# Windows user of the shipped CLI. A test-local normalisation would have made
# CI green and left that in place, unseen.
#
# This changes no committed bytes: `git ls-files --eol` reports i/lf w/lf for
# every tracked file today, so this pins behaviour that already holds rather
# than renormalising anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Detected as binary by `text=auto` anyway; named so that a corrupted one is a
# bug in the file rather than a question about this file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.dylib binary
*.so binary
*.a binary
*.aot binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
